The breakdown in a reverse-biased <span class="math-tex">\(\mathrm{p\text-n}\)</span> junction is more likely to occur due to:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td>the large velocity of the minority charge carriers if the doping concentration is small.</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td>the large velocity of the minority charge carriers if the doping concentration is large.</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td>strong electric field in a depletion region if the doping concentration is small.</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td>strong electric field in the depletion region if the doping concentration is large.</td></tr></tbody></table>

<p class="ParaOverride-94 caption" lang="en-US" style="text-align: left;" xml:lang="en-US">Choose the correct option:<br>1. (a), (d)<br>2. (b), (d)<br>3. (c), (d)<br>4. (b), (c)</p>
